From ea6a9ce6e0fa318ba025276003bf38128de5f2ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Message-Id: <cobiplayer-9006-mediacodec-window-gone@localhost>
From: Cobi Player <build@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:17:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mediacodec: a window gone as the decoder opens no longer
 crashes it

Before Android 10 (no ASurfaceControl, so no AImageReader) the decoder
renders straight to the app's window: CreateSurface. When that window is
gone as the decoder opens, CreateSurface releases the video context it has
just created. The context's destroy, CleanFromLegacyVideoContext, takes the
decoder from avctx->dec_opaque, which CreateSurface sets only once the
surface is ready, and the context's memory comes from malloc: it locks a
mutex through garbage. A SurfaceTexture that cannot be made takes the same
path.

Seen in Cobi Player on an Android 9 emulator: the app closed the player,
its views detached, while the video decoder opened. "Could not find a valid
ANativeWindow", then SIGSEGV in vlc_mutex_lock on the decoder's thread
(fault addr 0x11e: dec_opaque held 0x2a, the lock is at 0xf0).

- CreateSurface sets dec_opaque to NULL right after it creates the context.
- CleanFromLegacyVideoContext returns when it finds no decoder: OpenDecoder's
  bailout cleans the decoder itself, as before.
- A debug line ("no surface: the video context goes before the decoder used
  it") marks the error path and lets Cobi Player's package check see the
  patch in the build.

Nothing changes once the surface is ready. Not upstream: VLC master
(9c35ded8, 19.11.2026) has the same CreateSurface and
CleanFromLegacyVideoContext.
---
 modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c b/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c
index 4b8023d..6a15827 100644
--- a/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c
+++ b/modules/codec/omxil/mediacodec.c
@@ -727,6 +727,9 @@ static void CleanFromLegacyVideoContext(void *priv)
     android_video_context_t *avctx = priv;
     decoder_sys_t *p_sys = avctx->dec_opaque;
 
+    if (p_sys == NULL)
+        return; /* CreateSurface failed: OpenDecoder's bailout cleans the decoder */
+
     assert(!p_sys->video.use_air);
 
     vlc_mutex_lock(&p_sys->lock);
@@ -1036,6 +1039,9 @@ CreateSurface(decoder_t *p_dec, vlc_decoder_device *dec_dev,
 
     android_video_context_t *avctx =
         vlc_video_context_GetPrivate(p_sys->video.ctx, VLC_VIDEO_CONTEXT_AWINDOW);
+    /* The context's memory is not zeroed: until the surface is ready, its
+     * destroy must find no decoder to clean (the error path releases it). */
+    avctx->dec_opaque = NULL;
 
     if (!use_surfacetexture)
     {
@@ -1081,6 +1087,7 @@ end:
     return VLC_SUCCESS;
 
 error:
+    msg_Dbg(p_dec, "no surface: the video context goes before the decoder used it");
     vlc_video_context_Release(p_sys->video.ctx);
     p_sys->video.ctx = NULL;
     return VLC_EGENERIC;
